      "problem": "What is the volume of a sphere whose diameter is $9\\,\\text{m}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We can find the volume of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nV=\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting $r=\\frac{9}{2}\\,\\text{m}$ into the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nV=\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {(\\frac{9}{2})}^{3}=\\frac{243}{2}\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{3}.\n$$",
